      en: "The 14th July Bridge in Baghdad, named after the date of the 1958 Iraqi revolution, is another major Tigris crossing. Built in the 1960s, it connects al-Jadriya and al-Mansour districts. The bridge is known for its modern design and strategic importance. It suffered heavy damage during the 2003 invasion and was later renovated. Today, it serves as a central traffic hub, handling thousands of vehicles daily.",
