      en: "Qasr al-Salam (Palace of Peace) is one of Saddam Hussein's former presidential palaces in Baghdad. Built in the 1990s on the banks of the Tigris, the palace is an example of monumental architecture blending traditional and modern elements. The palace includes extensive gardens and ornate interiors. After 2003, it was used by the US military and later handed over to the Iraqi government. Today, it is partially open to the public and serves as an event venue.",
